[thin] These shortest approaches occur at the 3.00 mm fin landing's rounded/front edges and its 7 by 4 mm connecting brace. The tiny endpoint reading is a local joint termination, not a 0.018 mm nominal platform. The entire underside is reachable with H alone in its separately supported print. Physical reproduction of the small termini and platform handling capacity are unrecorded.
alternatives: A4.00 or 6.00 mm fin platform and a larger blended brace enlarge the joint but change the clearance to the stored R45 roof and need its access/removal review. Square or broader plate edges add corner stock with a larger footprint. Separate broad fin pedestals replace the bridge/platform with more pieces and a different form.
