[thin] These picks approach upper loop/pod and GR-cup-brace intersections or rounded cup corners. The local finite tapers meet the 7 by 4 mm ribbon/brace and the 2.70 mm roof/3.00 mm cup walls; they are not all a uniform 1 mm wall. Small boundary material can be lost or need cleanup, while the full members remain connected. H is separately supported; there is no physical strength, cleanup or repeated-handling acceptance.
alternatives: Larger 4–6 mm local blended overlaps/elbow pads or a 3.50 mm cup roof add stock while retaining its open entry, but need a new world -X grip-removal/source-sample access review. A solid broad upper frame eliminates many termini while obscuring more of the reference. Trimming tapered tips changes the boundary without making the connected member thicker.
