[thin] These are the repeated radial-strut/ribbon terminations at the 45-degree sample stations. The source strut has local X 5–21.5, Y ±3.5, Z -11–-7 (7 by 4 mm), posed RX -25° into the radius 70 ribbon. The minima are real finite tapers at their boundaries, not uniform submillimetre spanning walls. Independent exact sections at the 0.137/0.163 representative picks reach 4.00 mm vertical stock 1 mm inward toward the ribbon center; the 0.336/0.522 representatives reach 4.17/4.35 mm after 0.25 mm. Boundary material may be lost or need cleanup in printing. No strength, cleanup or handling-life acceptance is recorded.
alternatives: Larger 10–12 mm local elbow pads 4–6 mm thick or blended overlaps can enlarge these termini while retaining the moving seat, but add stock in the reviewed source-sample/removal envelopes and require renewed access/path review. Enlarging the entire ribbon/strut changes its occupied radius and cooling/support area. Trimming the small tapers can remove their tips but does not enlarge the joint.
