[thin] These picks are the R6 landing/brace union edges. The 7 by 4 mm brace meets a 3.00 mm landing; the small cap is backed by joined stock, with a representative 0.25 mm inward vertical section spanning Z 21.054–27.827. This is the reference storage joint, not the source expanding-R6 surface or a physical load qualification.
alternatives: A4.00 mm landing or a larger 10–12 mm elbow pad/blend enlarges the union but changes stock inside the surveyed seating/removal envelope. A full bed-rooted column replaces the joint with more material and blocks source round access. A separate large saddle adds another interface and part.
