[thin] These pairs approach different root/junction surface boundaries beside open regions. At the cached pair midpoints the exact STEP is outside, including Z offsets of -0.01 and +0.01 mm; these closest surface distances do not define a solid slab between the two points. The members join through neighboring root/brace stock. This scoped occupancy distinction is not a strength, stiffness or cleanup claim.
alternatives: A filled elbow or larger solid root can occupy more of these openings and add stock, but changes the source-sample access and needs the storage/removal paths reviewed. Broader blended unions change the local boundaries with additional material. Increasing the gap is another layout choice and does not thicken these existing members.
