[thin] These picks read the fluted apron's crest/end lands, not full thin walls:4.00 mm field grooves on 5.1221 mm pitch leave 1.1221 mm interior crest widths, with 1.20 mm depth and 5.80 mm intact backing in the 7.00 mm wall. The 2.20 mm end reading belongs to its outside field margin. This short field preserves the machine's profile vocabulary; it is not full-enclosure print or strength acceptance.
alternatives: A6.00 mm pitch gives 2.00 mm interior crests;3.00 mm groove width at the current pitch gives 2.1221 mm crests. Each changes the surface profile being referenced. An 8.50 mm wall increases backing to 7.30 mm but does not widen the crests and adds material/support exposure.
