[thin] This 2.311 mm closest approach lies in the swept R6-to-root brace elbow. The authored loft uses 7.00 mm planar width and 4.00 mm vertical stock; a shortest distance across its inclined/curving boundary need not equal that vertical section. It is carrier brace stock, not a calibration skin or source flexure. The separately supported assembly has no physical strength or repeated-handling qualification.
alternatives: A9 by 6 mm sweep or a broad 4–6 mm elbow pad increases the section while changing support/cooling and the neighboring reference-access envelope. A straighter brace with larger solid stock changes the form and needs revised seating/removal clearance. A full column adds stock and footprint while blocking more of the open source references.
file: hardware/printed-parts/calibration/soda-studies/parts/h-fluted-helix-and-keyed-fin-docks.step
