[thin] This 2.531 mm pair approaches the apron's top/front boundary and the fin-platform underside at Y 43. The exact midpoint and checkedZ offsets -0.10,-0.01,0,+0.01,+0.10 mm are outside the STEP. The local opening is air between stock regions connected elsewhere in H, not a 2.531 mm platform wall. The platform itself is 3.00 mm thick; the apron retains 5.80 mm backing beneath its field grooves.
alternatives: A larger filled elbow backs this opening but adds stock near the R45/fin access and needs a new removal review. Extending the apron upward closes this space while changing the field/root boundary. A lower platform changes its stored specimens' positions rather than correcting a material-thickness defect here.
file: hardware/printed-parts/calibration/soda-studies/parts/h-fluted-helix-and-keyed-fin-docks.step
