[thin] These opposite surfaces bound the actual 2.70 mm GR storage-cup roof. It is separate from the source grip and its wing slots and remains open on world -X and underneath for insertion/removal and automatic support access. The connected 7 by 4 mm brace adds local stock at its end; this roof's physical removal, stability and handling life are unmeasured.
alternatives: A3.50 or 6.00 mm roof adds outward stock while preserving the interior, but changes the brace/cup height envelope and needs the independently removable grip path reviewed. A broad upper cradle without a roof removes this ceiling but changes its locating/capture arrangement. A separate stand gives larger stock with another member and more footprint.
file: hardware/printed-parts/calibration/soda-studies/parts/h-fluted-helix-and-keyed-fin-docks.step
