[thin] These exact pairs bound 3.00 mm nominal pod, cup, fin-platform or root seating stock. They are structural/storage members of H, separate from the calibration skins, flexures and release-air ladders. The pods preserve 6.50 by 8.50 mm cavities for 6 by 8 mm removable keys, and the source-sample clearance envelope is kept open. These dimensions and sampled storage routes do not establish load or lifetime.
alternatives: Wider 4.00 or 6.00 mm stock can grow outward while preserving each cavity, but occupies the source/sample-access and reviewed individual-removal envelopes. Broad continuous platforms enlarge the sections while hiding more of the specimen surfaces and requiring new clearance review. Separately supported docks can use larger blocks at the cost of joints, parts and footprint.
